<title>FRANCE: BIS posts 1996 loss.</title>
<headline>BIS posts 1996 loss.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>French interim work company BIS, in which Dutch Vendex has 93.6 percent, said it had posted a 1996 net attributable loss of 106 million francs against a profit of 200 million in 1995.</p>
<p>Sales were down by 6.5 percent to 8.572 billion.</p>
<p>It said sales were up again at the start of 1997.</p>
</text>
